[Chapter "Two Knights (3...Nf6)"]
[Line "Quiet 4.d3 against ...Be7"]
[Opening "Italian Game: Two Knights Defense, Modern Bishop's Opening"]

{The calm way against the Two Knights: protect e4 and play the same build-up as in the Pianissimo.} 1. e4 {Take the centre and open lines for the queen and the f1 bishop.} 1... e5 2. Nf3 {Develop with an attack on e5.} 2... Nc6 3. Bc4 {The Italian: the bishop aims at f7, the weakest square in Black's camp.} 3... Nf6 {Black counterattacks e4.} 4. d3 {Calm and solid: protect e4 and keep the game in Italian structures.} 4... Be7 5. O-O {Castle.} 5... O-O 6. Re1 {Support e4.} 6... d6 7. a4 {Gain queenside space, a typical Pianissimo move.} *
